## 9. Install `uv`

> Installation commands can change over time. Use the current official `uv` installation documentation or an organization-approved package source. The commands below show the typical workflow, but project documentation takes priority.

### 9.1 Check Whether `uv` Is Already Installed

```powershell
uv --version
```

If a version is displayed, continue to project synchronization.

### 9.2 Install on Windows

A commonly used PowerShell installation pattern is:

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy ByPass -c "irm https://astral.sh/uv/install.ps1 | iex"
```

Security considerations:

- Confirm that the domain and command match the current official documentation.
- In a managed workstation, prefer the approved package manager or software center.
- Understand that this command downloads and executes an installation script.
- Do not run a remotely supplied script from an unverified source.

After installation, close and reopen PowerShell, then verify:

```powershell
uv --version
```

### 9.3 Verify the Executable Location

```powershell
Get-Command uv
```

If `uv` was installed but is not recognized, restart the terminal and check whether its installation directory was added to `PATH`.

