## 16. Responsible Use of AI Coding Assistants

AI coding tools are useful for explaining errors, suggesting commands, generating starter code, and identifying likely causes. Their output can still be incorrect, insecure, obsolete, or incompatible with the project.

Before following an AI suggestion:

1. Read the full command.
2. Identify files, permissions, and services it will affect.
3. Check the official project documentation.
4. Verify package and command names.
5. Avoid disabling SSL, antivirus, access controls, or security checks.
6. Do not paste credentials, proprietary code, or production data into unapproved tools.
7. Run destructive operations only after creating a backup or clean Git checkpoint.
8. Test the smallest safe change first.

Be especially cautious with commands containing:

```text
Remove-Item -Recurse -Force
rm -rf
Invoke-Expression
iex
ExecutionPolicy ByPass
curl ... | shell
administrator or sudo elevation
```

These commands are not automatically malicious, but they require additional review because they can execute remote code, bypass a local policy for a process, or delete large amounts of data.

