## 19. Repository Hygiene

A learning repository may use a structure such as:

```text
llm-learning-project/
├── .env.example
├── .gitignore
├── .python-version
├── README.md
├── pyproject.toml
├── uv.lock
├── docs/
│   ├── environment-setup.md
│   ├── troubleshooting.md
│   └── learning-log.md
├── notebooks/
│   └── first_llm_experiment.ipynb
├── src/
│   └── app/
│       ├── __init__.py
│       ├── config.py
│       └── main.py
└── tests/
    └── test_config.py
```

Recommended commit sequence:

```powershell
git status
git add README.md docs .gitignore .env.example
git commit -m "Document LLM development environment setup"
```

Review staged files before committing:

```powershell
git diff --staged
```

Never use `git add .` without reviewing what it will stage, especially when working with notebooks, outputs, datasets, logs, and environment files.

